OL,3,GNEWSA'You can wait thousands of hours
OL,4,Afor the perfect shot'
OL,5,
OL,6,FAs a polar explorer, Conrad Dickinson
OL,7,Fhas found himself face-to-face with
OL,8,Farctic wolves and even got the chance
OL,9,Fto photograph polar bears, arctic foxes
OL,10,Fand other amazing wildlife.
OL,12,FYet, he still loves to spend hours in
OL,13,Fthe moorlands of his native North East
OL,14,Fand nearby Cumbria, patiently waiting
OL,15,Fto catch a glimpse of a hen harrier or
OL,16,Fa short-eared owl.
OL,18,F"Very often with bird photography, it
OL,19,Finvolves hundreds if not thousands of
OL,20,Fhours sitting just waiting when nothing
OL,21,Fhappens," says the 71-year-old from
OL,22,FHexham.
OL,23,APub: 27-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NE Eng NewsC Reg TVF Weather
